# Rust build artifacts
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
target

# --- POLICY CHANGE: Cargo.lock is now ignored (was previously committed) ---
# Previously this repository intentionally tracked the root Cargo.lock, on the
# grounds that oxiz-cli ships as a binary crate and reproducible binary builds
# want a committed lockfile.
# That policy has been reversed: OxiZ is primarily consumed as a set of library
# crates published to crates.io, where the lockfile is ignored by downstream
# users anyway, and a tracked lockfile produces constant merge conflicts and
# churn on every dependency bump (Latest crates policy).
# CI and release builds should pin dependencies explicitly when reproducibility
# is required, rather than relying on a committed lockfile.
# Do NOT re-add Cargo.lock to version control.
# Root-anchored on purpose: per-crate lockfiles (fuzz, bench/z3_parity) stay tracked.
/Cargo.lock
/bench/z3_parity/results.json
/bench/z3_parity/results.*.json

